1
00:00:00,782 --> 00:00:04,640
大家好，欢迎来到本周 AI 快报。
Hello everyone and welcome to This Week in AI.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,516
我是 Vicky Raiselman，很高兴今天能和大家见面。
My name is Vicky Raiselman, and I'm excited to be with you today.

3
00:00:08,974 --> 00:00:10,400
那么，我该怎么跟你们说呢？
Well, what can I tell you?

4
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:12,836
上周真是太疯狂了。
Last week was a doozy.

5
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:21,060
我们收到的新闻全都指向一个核心点，那就是 AI Agent。
We had news coming about one thing and one thing only, and that was AI agents.

6
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:26,020
它们在做坏事，也在做好事，而且还有各种各样的行为。
They were doing the bad, they were doing the good, and everything in between.

7
00:00:26,254 --> 00:00:29,988
所以今天的每周新闻将重点关注它们。
And so our weekly news today will focus on them.

8
00:00:30,574 --> 00:00:33,120
那么，概括一下，我们今天要涵盖哪些内容？
So at a glance, what are we going to cover today?

9
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:35,680
首先，我们要从我最喜欢的话题开始。
Well, we're going to start with my favorite topic.

10
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:39,680
如果你以前看过我的视频，你会发现我非常热爱网络安全。
If you've seen me on here before, I absolutely love cybersecurity.

11
00:00:39,918 --> 00:00:48,100
我上周大部分时间都在处理影响各大网站的 PHP 漏洞。
And I've spent most of last week working on the PHP vulnerability that hit major sites.

12
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:54,080
这些网站当然也是我所在公司 Akamai 的客户。
And were, of course, Akamai customers, the company that I work for.

13
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:59,060
我会告诉你们我们做了什么，我们需要思考什么，以及为什么它与其他漏洞不同。
I'll tell you what we did, what we need to think about, and why it's different than any other.

14
00:00:59,214 --> 00:01:02,480
接下来，我们当然会进入安全与治理领域。
where they're going to, of course, move into safety and governance.

15
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:10,800
嘿，既然这些 Agent 现在开始失控，而且我们正在利
用各种漏洞，我们能做些什么，目前的情况又如何？
And hey, now that these agents are going rogue and we're exploiting all kinds of vulnerabilities,
what can we do about it and what's happening there?

16
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:15,748
当然，AI 没电是跑不起来的。
And of course, AI cannot run without electricity.

17
00:01:16,654 --> 00:01:33,284
我们要聊聊 NVIDIA，以及他们正投入近 1650 亿美元建设数据中心，
基本上是把数据中心当成银行来支持这个 Agent 生态系统。
And we're going to go into NVIDIA and the fact that they're spending almost $165 billion building data centers,
backing up data centers as a bank, essentially, so we can support this agentic ecosystem.

18
00:01:33,998 --> 00:01:36,080
但我想带给大家更多乐观的色彩。
But I want to leave us with more optimism.

19
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:46,180
我认为在健康、科学以及药物研发和一些新发明方面，有很多值得乐观的发展。
And I think there's a lot of optimism to be had with health and science and
some of the developments when it comes to drugs and new inventions there.

20
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:51,716
当然，如果不聊聊消费端和企业端的 Agent，我就做得不完整了。
And of course, I would be remiss not to cover consumer and enterprise agents.

21
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:54,560
如果你还没听说过 Muse，它是免费的。
If you haven't heard of Muse, it's free.

22
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:56,868
去搜一下，去试用一下。
Look it up and try it out.

23
00:01:57,326 --> 00:02:10,211
现在，当我查看各大消费品牌和旅游网站的客户网站数据时，
Meta 在流量数量上实际上仅排在 OpenAI 之后。
Now, when I'm looking at customer website data across major consumer brands and travel websites,
Meta Muse is actually only second in terms of the number of traffic compared to OpenAI.

24
00:02:10,574 --> 00:02:11,360
嘿，谁知道呢？
Hey, who knows?

25
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:12,484
也许我会夺过领先地位。
Maybe I'll take the lead.

26
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:16,640
那么，让我们从网络安全开始。
So let's start with cybersecurity.

27
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:27,172
这里的第一个项目不是你预想中的 PHP 漏洞（虽然我
之后会花大量时间讲它），而是 RTEX Agentic AI。
And the first item here is not the PHP vulnerability, which you would expect, which
I'm going to actually spend a lot of time on, but it's actually the RTEX agentic AI.

28
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:35,588
这是一次供应链攻击，利用了超过 2000 个 Microsoft 租户。
And it was a supply chain attack that exploited over 2,000 Microsoft tenants.

29
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,920
为什么这很重要呢？
And why is it so important?

30
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:49,796
我希望你们注意的不是它是一个开源的多智能体渗透测试框架，
而是这个框架在这次攻击中基本上被利用了。
I want you to pay attention not to the fact that it's open source and
multi-agent pen testing framework that got essentially exploited in this attack.

31
00:02:50,286 --> 00:02:51,812
但到底是什么被利用了？
But what got exploited?

32
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:58,160
被利用的是 OAuth 应用程序。
What got exploited is OAuth applications.

33
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:05,360
OAuth 基本上让我们能够识别谁进入了我们的网络。
OAuth essentially has allowed us to identify who is coming into our network.

34
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:14,084
而且多因素身份验证从未真正被应用，而它本来应该是为了让我们的身份验证更安全。
And multi-factor authentication was never actually applied, which is supposed to make our authentication more secure.

35
00:03:15,982 --> 00:03:17,360
为什么这很重要？
Why is this important?

36
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:34,084
原因是我们长期依赖的身份识别和安全方法，用于让系统通信并保护我们的基础设施，
现在正暴露在这些 Agent 手中。
The reason is the identification and security methods we long relied on to have our
systems communicate to protect our infrastructure are now exposed by these agents.

37
00:03:36,366 --> 00:03:38,692
这意味着存在一个机会。
And this means there's an opportunity.

38
00:03:39,088 --> 00:03:42,688
我们的观众里有非常优秀的顶尖技术人才。
We have an incredible audience here of top technical talent.

39
00:03:42,848 --> 00:03:51,332
我想说的是，这是一个重新定义今天互联网上身份真正含义的机会吗？
And what I would say is what is this opportunity to redefine what identity really means on the internet today?

40
00:03:53,358 --> 00:04:00,688
现在我要深入探讨一下 PHP to shell 攻击，因为大家可能都已经听说过了。
Now I'm going to dive deeper into the PHP to shell attack because everyone has probably heard about it.

41
00:04:00,848 --> 00:04:05,088
PHP 本质上就是 PHP HTTP 协议。
PHP is essentially PHP hypertext protocol.

42
00:04:05,408 --> 00:04:12,260
目前超过 70% 的网站都在使用这种协议。
Over 70%, 70% of websites use this protocol today.

43
00:04:12,910 --> 00:04:23,876
这就是为什么这是一个极其巨大的漏洞，遍布在几乎每一个网站上。
This is why this is an incredibly huge vulnerability that landed across every, almost every website.

44
00:04:24,448 --> 00:04:41,572
不仅如此，最早暴露的欧洲政府网站不仅泄露了密码和 MFA 密钥，
而且这一切都在攻击被发现后的两小时内就发生了。
Not only that, the European government website that was exposed first exposed not just passwords and MFA secrets,
and all of that happened within two hours of that attack being identified.

45
00:04:43,054 --> 00:04:57,156
正如我提到的，我在一家叫 Akamai 的公司工作，当时我就在第一线，
客户开始致电我们的运营中心，报告一级严重攻击。
So as I mentioned, I work for a company called Akamai, And I was kind of at the front lines when this occurred,
and customers started calling in with severity one attacks to our operations center.

46
00:04:58,190 --> 00:04:59,328
这造成了巨大的混乱。
It caused havoc.

47
00:04:59,568 --> 00:05:06,436
我们联系了负责为我们的防火墙制定保护规则的威胁研究团队。
We went to our threat research team that puts together these protection rules for our firewall.

48
00:05:06,608 --> 00:05:10,608
我们问他们，有没有什么我们可以为这些客户开启的防护措施？
And we said, Do you have something for us that we can turn on for these customers?

49
00:05:10,768 --> 00:05:12,932
我们正受到来自不同方向的攻击。
We're getting hit from different directions.

50
00:05:14,094 --> 00:05:23,088
我们花了几个小时，但我们最终还是成功开启了这条规则，基本上阻止了这类攻击。
And it took us a few hours, but we did able, we were able to turn on this rule and deny,
essentially preventing from this type of attack.

51
00:05:23,248 --> 00:05:25,168
那么，为什么这次攻击很重要呢？
Now, why is this attack important?

52
00:05:27,342 --> 00:05:28,688
想象一下一名服务员。
Imagine a waiter.

53
00:05:29,008 --> 00:05:38,052
你带着 20 人的大家庭去餐厅，每个人都有不同的饮食需求和特殊要求。
You bring your large extended family of 20 people to the restaurant, and everyone has their dietary needs and special requirements.

54
00:05:38,368 --> 00:05:46,288
你按顺序绕桌子走，你的妻子说，噢，我真的很想吃那
份鸡肉，但我想要烤的，而且旁边只配米饭和西兰花。
And you go around the table in order, and your wife says, Oh, I really want that chicken,
but I want it grilled and only rice and broccoli on the side.

55
00:05:46,368 --> 00:05:50,048
你的儿子说，我对乳糖过敏。
And your son says, I have an allergy to lactose.

56
00:05:50,128 --> 00:05:51,728
我能喝无乳糖牛奶吗？
Can I have lactose-free milk?

57
00:05:51,888 --> 00:05:53,168
这种情况一直持续到第 20 个人。
And this continues for 20.

58
00:05:53,408 --> 00:05:56,804
突然之间，服务员完全崩溃了。
And all of a sudden, the waiter gets absolutely overwhelmed.

59
00:05:57,710 --> 00:06:00,128
这个订单完全不寻常。
The order is completely unusual.

60
00:06:00,288 --> 00:06:05,648
所以，因为服务员压力太大，在这种情况下就是 PHP，对吧？
And so, because the waiter gets so overwhelmed, in this case it's PHP, right?

61
00:06:06,126 --> 00:06:09,488
它开始做的就是把这些信息以随机的顺序吐出来。
What it starts doing is spewing this information back in random order.

62
00:06:09,648 --> 00:06:20,368
它开始，噢，呃，是那个需要西兰花和鸡肉的孩子，还
是那个需要那个订单，嗯，是不是乳糖不耐受的妻子？
It starts, oh, uh, was that the child that needed the broccoli and the chicken,
or the wife that needed that order with um was it lactose intolerance?

63
00:06:20,528 --> 00:06:21,412
我不记得了。
I can't remember.

64
00:06:21,934 --> 00:06:28,688
所以，就服务员的情况来说，现在他们返回的是之前告诉它的信息。
So, in the case of the waiter, right, now they're giving back the information about what was told to it.

65
00:06:28,768 --> 00:06:33,568
而这些信息，不幸的是，不再是食物订单了，对吧？
And that information, unfortunately, is no longer the food order, right?

66
00:06:33,838 --> 00:06:46,084
在这种情况下，它返回的是关于密码、API 安全令
牌以及各种它不该泄露的信息，因为它完全崩溃了。
In this case, it's giving back random information about passwords and API security tokens and all kinds of things it shouldn't have
given out because it's completely overwhelmed.

67
00:06:46,928 --> 00:06:55,972
这对这些公司意味着，有人可能会获得运行他们 Web 应用程序的服务器访问权限。
What this meant for these companies is someone could get access to the servers that run their web applications.

68
00:06:56,366 --> 00:07:02,052
那是 70% 的数字，记住那个，而且没有任何类型的身份验证。
That's 70% number, remember that, without any type of authentication.

69
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:06,928
另外，想想这个漏洞发生的极快速度。
Also, think about the speed with which this occurred, this vulnerability.

70
00:07:07,088 --> 00:07:13,088
严重程度等级为 9.2 分，直到 10 月 21 日才被披露。
9.2 out of 10 severity scale was only revealed on October 21st.

71
00:07:13,168 --> 00:07:17,488
而我们发现它的唯一原因是因为 Mythos。
And we the only reason it was found was because of Mythos.

72
00:07:17,966 --> 00:07:31,044
如果你还记得，Mythos 是一个安全模型，它能够提取所有这些不同类型的 PHP 版本，
并且实际上通过将不同漏洞拼接在一起，创建出这种类型的攻击。
If you remember, Mythos is a security model that was able to pull all these different types of versions of PHB and actually,
by stitching things together with different vulnerabilities, create this type of attack.

73
00:07:31,488 --> 00:07:34,660
这仅靠人类是永远无法发现的。
This could have never been discovered by humans alone.

74
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:38,048
欢迎 AI 智能体。
Welcome, AI agents.

75
00:07:38,288 --> 00:07:39,428
非常感谢。
Thank you very much.

76
00:07:40,366 --> 00:07:50,208
共有 2260 万个实例暴露在外，我们仍在继续处理这类后果。
22.6 million instances were exposed and we're continuing to deal with this type of ramification.

77
00:07:50,288 --> 00:08:01,540
现在，拥有足够资源的跨国大公司可以购买额外的安全工具，在企业内部真正推动零信任理念。
Now, large companies that have the resources in place they can buy additional
security tools to really drive the zero trust mindset within their enterprise.

78
00:08:04,174 --> 00:08:17,632
然而，规模较小的企业，比如可能只运营一个博客或小型电商网站的，
现在必须想办法修复那些服务器，因为他们的客户信息已经泄露了。
However, smaller businesses, you know, that might have run a blog or just a small commerce site now have to figure out how to patch
those servers because their customers' information is exposed.

79
00:08:17,792 --> 00:08:25,732
我总是为那些小企业感到难受，因为他们往往没有大公司那样的资源。
And I always feel worse for the little guy because they don't have the resources often of the larger companies.

80
00:08:26,094 --> 00:08:29,956
这是我们绝对需要继续关注的事情。
This is something that we definitely need to continue to watch.

81
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:34,020
但这里还有另一个新闻。
But here's another news.

82
00:08:35,566 --> 00:08:47,108
公司正在试图搞清楚，不仅是那些试图黑入并回溯信息的智能体，
还有那些代表我们进行购买的智能体。
Companies are trying to figure out, not just with the agents that are trying to hack and backtrack the information,
but the agents that are trying to purchase on our behalf.

83
00:08:47,726 --> 00:08:59,300
像 Walmart 这样的公司不想放弃这些智能体带来的收入，但与此同时，他们必须保护安全。
Companies like Walmart do not want to give up the income that will come from these agents, but at the same time, they have to protect.

84
00:09:00,032 --> 00:09:04,196
因此，Walmart 刚刚发布了一个智能体网关。
And so Walmart just released an agent gateway.

85
00:09:05,294 --> 00:09:12,676
基本上，智能体网关是一个 MCP 服务器，它允许经过授权的智能体代表客户购物。
Essentially, the agent gateway is an MCP server that lets approved agents shop for customers.

86
00:09:13,774 --> 00:09:26,340
所以现在维琪在 Walmart.com 上为她的 Meta 智能体、她的
Cloud 智能体以及她的 OpenAI GPT agent 拥有了个人资料。
So now Vicky has a profile within Walmart.com for her Meta agent, for her Cloud agent, her OpenAI Dots agent.

87
00:09:26,702 --> 00:09:28,836
而这些资料定义了
And these profiles define

88
00:09:31,790 --> 00:09:34,032
这些智能体能够做什么。
what those agents are able to do.

89
00:09:34,192 --> 00:09:36,592
它们能花多少钱？
How much are they able to spend?

90
00:09:36,832 --> 00:09:40,676
它们单次购买的审批范围和交易限额是多少？
What's the scope of their per-purchase approval and transaction?

91
00:09:41,632 --> 00:09:46,500
这实际上是运行时智能体控制的一个模板。
And really a template for runtime agent control.

92
00:09:46,912 --> 00:09:54,084
我可以告诉你们，因为我就在这个行业工作，其他大品牌也在关注类似的网关。
I can tell you because I work in this industry and other large brands are looking at a similar gateway.

93
00:09:54,638 --> 00:09:56,644
他们并不是想阻止智能体。
They're not trying to stop agents.

94
00:09:57,422 --> 00:10:14,980
以亚马逊为例，你们可能在上周听说了他们封锁了 Meta 智能体在他们网络上的访问，
但这并不是因为他们不想获得那部分购物量或收入。
In the case of Amazon, you probably heard the previous week that they blocked Meta agent on their network,
but that's not because I feel because they don't want that shopping volume or income.

95
00:10:15,310 --> 00:10:23,232
而是因为他们感到害怕，因为他们的整个广告营收
模式都是建立在人类在他们网站上购物的基础上的。
It's because they're afraid, because their whole advertising revenue model is built on human shopping on their site.

96
00:10:23,392 --> 00:10:24,592
想想你们是怎么购物的。
Think about how you shop.

97
00:10:24,752 --> 00:10:36,592
你会看推荐商品，看评论，你会因为一键下单、送货上门、
次日达这些原因在亚马逊上逛街和挑选，对吧？
You look at recommended items, you look at reviews, you look, you shop around
and browse on Amazon because of one click, delivery, one day delivery, right?

98
00:10:36,912 --> 00:10:56,388
所有这些让亚马逊变得伟大的因素，以及它占据互联网上超过 50% 的消费者购买流量，
现在成了 Walmart 夺回部分市场份额的机会。
All those things that made Amazon great and for it to have more than 50% of all consumer purchasing traffic on the internet is now an
opportunity for Walmart to take some of that market back.

99
00:10:56,846 --> 00:10:58,112
所以密切关注这一点。
So watch this closely.

100
00:10:58,272 --> 00:11:00,004
我认为它还会进一步演变。
I think it's going to evolve even more.

101
00:11:01,232 --> 00:11:02,884
简单总结一下。
So a quick summary.

102
00:11:03,470 --> 00:11:08,432
记住 PHP2 shell，关注它，和你的团队谈谈这件事。
Remember, PHP2 shell, pay attention to it, talk to your teams about it.

103
00:11:08,592 --> 00:11:10,564
这不是你可以忽视的。
This is not one you want to ignore.

104
00:11:10,862 --> 00:11:20,068
在严重程度等级上是 9.2 分，你要确保修复你的服务器，尤其是如果它们在使用 PHP 的话。
9.2 out of 10 on severity scale, you want to make sure that you patch your servers, especially if they're using PHP.

105
00:11:21,838 --> 00:11:23,472
还要记住时间线。
And remember the timelines.

106
00:11:23,632 --> 00:11:34,660
你已经没有时间去分析流量、去理解发生了什么，或
者在将其设为拒绝模式之前先在警报模式下观察了。
You no longer have the time to analyze the traffic, to understand what
happened, to watch it in alert mode before you put it in a deny mode.

107
00:11:35,150 --> 00:11:37,700
这一切都在不到两小时内发生。
All of that happens in less than two hours.

108
00:11:38,094 --> 00:11:52,772
Agentic AI attacker 只用了不到两小时，就从一个欧洲政府机构获取了密码、
哈希值和多因素身份验证系统的密钥。
Less than two hours was all it took for a Gentic AI tagger to grab the passwords, hashes,
and multi-factor authentication system secrets at a European government.

109
00:11:53,358 --> 00:11:57,072
这意味着人工操作的速度不够快了。
That means the human touch is not fast enough.

110
00:11:57,312 --> 00:12:04,752
我们每季度修复一定数量 CVE 漏洞的时代已经结束了。
The days of us patching our servers every quarter with a certain number of CVEs is over.

111
00:12:06,190 --> 00:12:21,860
